// in history Broke's ram (collisions wait for fighting.md 4.11). Two big leaders against six smaller, faster boats.
// History's forces; the classes are stand-ins (flotilla_leader for both leaders, v1 for the G37 and V25 boats, the
// smaller design, as the boats were smaller than the leaders), set for balance: the leaders' crews elite, the boats'
// average; even so the six are the favourites, as the AI plays it (the leaders lose about a ship a run, the boats one
// in two or three runs), and a player who combs the tracks does better:
//   Britain, the hammer: two 31 kn leaders with four 4 in each, the patrol's eyes on a moonless night.
//   Germany, the pack: six 33 kn boats, 88 mm guns, thirty-six tubes, heading home for Zeebrugge.
// The weather of the night: calm, overcast, no moon. In so black a night (docs/battle/night.md Q1) a boat is made out at a
// few hundred yards, so the two run into each other: the boats' course passes 300 m off the leaders' (it was 1.8 km for
// the old 5 km night).
